.metasync-inline-43 { border: 1px solid grey; border-collapse: collapse; }
.metasync-inline-44 { border: 1px solid grey; border-collapse: collapse; }</style>[/et_pb_code][et_pb_section fb_built="1" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}" ][et_pb_row _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"][et_pb_column type="4_4" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"] [et_pb_heading title="Therma-Tru Doors vs Codel Doors: A Complete Comparison Guide" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h1" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_image src="https://soundviewwindowanddoor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/stylish-fiberglass-entry-door-enhancing-home-aesthetics-46e4cfda-3bc5-42c9-8df6-2d34cf367d1f.jpg" url="https://soundviewwindowanddoor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/stylish-fiberglass-entry-door-enhancing-home-aesthetics-46e4cfda-3bc5-42c9-8df6-2d34cf367d1f.jpg" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" hover_enabled="0" global_colors_info="{}" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_image] [et_pb_heading title="Therma-Tru Doors vs Codel Doors: Complete Comparison Guide for Fiberglass Entry Doors" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">By Dan McLaughlin, Sound View Window &amp; Door</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_image src="https://soundviewwindowanddoor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/stylish-fiberglass-entry-door-enhancing-home-aesthetics-46e4cfda-3bc5-42c9-8df6-2d34cf367d1f.jpg" url="https://soundviewwindowanddoor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/stylish-fiberglass-entry-door-enhancing-home-aesthetics-46e4cfda-3bc5-42c9-8df6-2d34cf367d1f.jpg" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" hover_enabled="0" global_colors_info="{}" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_image][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">When it comes to choosing the right entry door for your home, the decision can be overwhelming due to the variety of options available. This guide provides a comprehensive comparison between Therma-Tru and Codel doors, two leading brands in the fiberglass entry door market. Homeowners, builders, and contractors will find valuable insights into the key differences, material durability, energy efficiency, and customization options of these two brands. Understanding these factors is crucial for making an informed decision that enhances both the aesthetic appeal and functionality of your home. This article will cover the main differences between Therma-Tru and Codel doors, their performance in energy efficiency, warranty options, and much more.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="What Are the Key Differences Between Therma-Tru and Codel Fiberglass Doors?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_image src="https://soundviewwindowanddoor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/comparison-of-therma-tru-and-codel-fiberglass-doors-showcasing-design-and-material-differences-d53e6606-92fc-4a7d-8fa2-23a332c1c236.jpg" url="https://soundviewwindowanddoor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/comparison-of-therma-tru-and-codel-fiberglass-doors-showcasing-design-and-material-differences-d53e6606-92fc-4a7d-8fa2-23a332c1c236.jpg" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" hover_enabled="0" global_colors_info="{}" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_image][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Therma-Tru and Codel doors are both popular choices for fiberglass entry doors, but they differ in several key aspects. Therma-Tru is known for its extensive range of styles and innovative designs, while Codel focuses on high-quality materials and craftsmanship. The primary differences include:</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<ul><li><strong>Material Composition</strong>: Therma-Tru doors often feature a composite material that enhances durability, while Codel doors utilize solid fiberglass for superior strength.</li><li><strong>Design Options</strong>: Therma-Tru offers a wider variety of styles and finishes, catering to diverse aesthetic preferences. Codel, on the other hand, emphasizes a more classic and timeless design approach.</li><li><strong>Performance Metrics</strong>: Both brands provide excellent thermal insulation, but their energy efficiency ratings may vary based on specific models.</li></ul>[/et_pb_code][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<table class="metasyncTable"><tr><th class="metasync-inline-2">Brand</th><th class="metasync-inline-3">Material</th><th class="metasync-inline-4">Design Variety</th><th class="metasync-inline-5">Energy Efficiency</th></tr><tr><td class="metasync-inline-6">Therma-Tru</td><td class="metasync-inline-7">Composite</td><td class="metasync-inline-8">High</td><td class="metasync-inline-9">Excellent</td></tr><tr><td class="metasync-inline-10">Codel</td><td class="metasync-inline-11">Solid Fiberglass</td><td class="metasync-inline-12">Moderate</td><td class="metasync-inline-13">Very Good</td></tr></table>[/et_pb_code][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">These differences highlight the unique strengths of each brand, helping consumers choose the best option for their needs.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="How Do Material Durability and Build Quality Compare?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Material durability and build quality are critical factors when selecting an entry door. Therma-Tru doors are engineered with a focus on long-lasting performance, utilizing advanced materials that resist warping and cracking. Codel doors, made from solid fiberglass, are also designed for durability, providing resistance to dents and scratches.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Indeed, the inherent strength of fiberglass is a key factor in its widespread use for durable entry doors.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<blockquote class="metasyncQuote"><strong>Fiberglass vs. Steel Doors: Durability &amp; Cost</strong><br><br>to durability, steel and fiberglass doors are at the top of the list since they are known for their strength and. Due to this increase in quality, fiberglass doors are a bit pricier than their steel<br><br>The Importance of Choosing Between Steel and Fiberglass Doors: Making the Best Choice for Your Home</blockquote>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Both brands undergo rigorous testing to ensure they meet high standards for quality and performance. Homeowners can expect both options to withstand the elements effectively, but the choice may come down to personal preference regarding material feel and finish.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="What Warranty Options Do Each Brand Offer?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Warranty options are essential for peace of mind when investing in a new entry door. Therma-Tru typically offers a limited lifetime warranty on their doors, covering defects in materials and workmanship. Codel also provides a robust warranty, often matching or exceeding industry standards, which includes coverage for fading and delamination.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Understanding the specifics of each warranty can help homeowners make a more informed decision, ensuring they choose a door that not only meets their aesthetic needs but also provides long-term protection.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="How Do Therma-Tru and Codel Doors Perform in Energy Efficiency?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">When choosing an entry door, energy efficiency directly affects your home's comfort and long-term utility costs. Both Therma-Tru and Codel manufacture fiberglass doors with insulating cores, but their performance ratings differ across product lines.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Therma-Tru Energy Efficiency" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Therma-Tru is one of the most tested and certified door brands for energy performance. Their doors feature a high-density polyurethane foam core that significantly outperforms wood and steel doors in thermal resistance.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">U-factor and SHGC ratings by product line (per manufacturer specifications):</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<ul><li><strong>Fiber-Classic Collection:</strong> U-factor 0.17–0.20 | SHGC 0.19–0.25 | ENERGY STAR certified for all U.S. climate zones</li><li><strong>Smooth-Star Collection:</strong> U-factor 0.17–0.21 | SHGC 0.18–0.27 | ENERGY STAR certified; most popular entry-level fiberglass line</li><li><strong>Pulse Collection:</strong> U-factor 0.16–0.19 | SHGC 0.17–0.22 | ENERGY STAR certified; designed for high-performance thermal efficiency</li><li><strong>Classic-Craft Collection:</strong> U-factor 0.17–0.20 | SHGC 0.19–0.24 | ENERGY STAR certified; premium woodgrain texture finish</li></ul>[/et_pb_code][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Insulation core: All Therma-Tru fiberglass slabs use a polyurethane foam core with an R-value of approximately R-5 to R-6 per inch, delivering significantly better insulation than hollow-core steel alternatives.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">ENERGY STAR certification: Therma-Tru doors with low-E glass and foam cores meet ENERGY STAR requirements across all four U.S. climate zones (Northern, North-Central, South-Central, and Southern).</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Codel Energy Efficiency" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Codel fiberglass entry doors also use an insulating foam core construction, providing solid thermal performance at a more accessible price point.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">U-factor and SHGC ratings by product line (per manufacturer specifications):</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<ul><li><strong>Codel Fiberglass Smooth:</strong> U-factor 0.20–0.27 | SHGC 0.21–0.30 | ENERGY STAR eligible with qualifying glass packages</li><li><strong>Codel Fiberglass Textured:</strong> U-factor 0.20–0.26 | SHGC 0.22–0.31 | ENERGY STAR eligible in most climate zones</li><li><strong>Codel Prefinished Fiberglass:</strong> U-factor 0.21–0.28 | SHGC 0.22–0.32 | Suitable for South-Central and Southern climate zones</li></ul>[/et_pb_code][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Insulation core: Codel fiberglass doors use a polyurethane foam core construction, with an approximate R-value of R-5 per inch — comparable to entry-level Therma-Tru lines but with slightly less consistency across their full product range.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">ENERGY STAR certification: Codel doors can qualify for ENERGY STAR certification depending on the glass package selected. Always verify the specific configuration with your dealer before purchase.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Side-by-Side Energy Efficiency Comparison" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_code _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<table class="metasyncTable"><tr><th class="metasync-inline-15">Metric</th><th class="metasync-inline-16">Therma-Tru (Best)</th><th class="metasync-inline-17">Therma-Tru (Typical)</th><th class="metasync-inline-18">Codel (Best)</th><th class="metasync-inline-19">Codel (Typical)</th></tr><tr><td class="metasync-inline-20">U-factor</td><td class="metasync-inline-21">0.16</td><td class="metasync-inline-22">0.17–0.21</td><td class="metasync-inline-23">0.20</td><td class="metasync-inline-24">0.20–0.28</td></tr><tr><td class="metasync-inline-25">SHGC</td><td class="metasync-inline-26">0.17</td><td class="metasync-inline-27">0.18–0.27</td><td class="metasync-inline-28">0.21</td><td class="metasync-inline-29">0.21–0.32</td></tr><tr><td class="metasync-inline-30">Foam Core R-value</td><td class="metasync-inline-31">R-6/inch</td><td class="metasync-inline-32">R-5 to R-6/inch</td><td class="metasync-inline-33">R-5/inch</td><td class="metasync-inline-34">~R-5/inch</td></tr><tr><td class="metasync-inline-35">ENERGY STAR Certified</td><td class="metasync-inline-36">Yes (all zones)</td><td class="metasync-inline-37">Yes</td><td class="metasync-inline-38">Yes (select configs)</td><td class="metasync-inline-39">Varies by glass pkg</td></tr><tr><td class="metasync-inline-40">Climate Zone Coverage</td><td class="metasync-inline-41">All 4 U.S. zones</td><td class="metasync-inline-42">All 4 U.S. zones</td><td class="metasync-inline-43">Most zones</td><td class="metasync-inline-44">South-Central/Southern</td></tr></table>[/et_pb_code][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara"><em>Note: Lower U-factor = better insulation. Lower SHGC = less solar heat gain. All values are based on manufacturer-published specifications and may vary by glass package, frame configuration, and installation method. Always confirm current ratings directly with the manufacturer or your door dealer.</em></p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="What Are the Latest Energy Star Ratings and Certifications?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Energy Star ratings are crucial indicators of a door's energy efficiency. Both Therma-Tru and Codel doors have models that meet or exceed Energy Star certification requirements. This certification signifies that the doors have been tested and verified to provide superior energy performance, helping homeowners save on heating and cooling costs.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Further research into the material science behind these doors confirms the effectiveness of fiberglass in achieving high thermal performance.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<blockquote class="metasyncQuote"><strong>Fiberglass Insulation: Thermal Performance Analysis</strong><br><br>thermal conductivity can be used with confidence to estimate the thermal performance of fiberglass insulation. This paper is to show how the thermal performance of a fibrous insulation, as<br><br><span class="cite-source">Effective thermal conductivity of fiberglass insulation, MK Choudhary, 2024</span></blockquote>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="How Do Energy Efficient Entry Doors Impact Home Performance?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Investing in energy-efficient entry doors can significantly impact overall home performance. These doors help reduce energy consumption, leading to lower utility bills and a smaller carbon footprint. Additionally, energy-efficient doors can enhance indoor comfort by minimizing drafts and temperature fluctuations.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Homeowners can expect improved energy efficiency ratings when upgrading to either Therma-Tru or Codel doors, making them a smart choice for those looking to enhance their home's performance.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="What Style and Customization Options Are Available for Each Brand?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Both Therma-Tru and Codel offer a range of style and customization options to suit various architectural designs. Therma-Tru is particularly known for its extensive selection of door styles, including traditional, contemporary, and rustic designs. Homeowners can choose from various finishes, colors, and decorative glass options to create a personalized look.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Codel, while offering fewer styles, focuses on high-quality finishes and classic designs that appeal to those seeking timeless elegance. Customization options may include hardware choices and specific sizing to fit unique entryways.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Which Door Designs and Finishes Do Therma-Tru and Codel Offer?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Therma-Tru provides a diverse array of door designs, including options with intricate glass patterns and various panel configurations. Their finishes range from rich wood grains to modern solid colors, allowing homeowners to find the perfect match for their home’s exterior.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Codel doors, while more limited in design variety, offer high-quality finishes that emphasize durability and aesthetic appeal. Their focus on craftsmanship ensures that each door is not only functional but also visually striking.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="How Do Door Security Features Compare?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Security is a paramount concern for homeowners when selecting an entry door. Both Therma-Tru and Codel doors are designed with security in mind, featuring robust locking mechanisms and reinforced frames.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Therma-Tru doors often include multi-point locking systems that enhance security, while Codel doors are built with solid fiberglass that provides additional strength against forced entry. Homeowners can feel confident in the security features offered by both brands.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="What Are the Pricing and Installation Considerations for Therma-Tru vs Codel Doors?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Pricing for Therma-Tru and Codel doors can vary based on the specific model and customization options chosen. Generally, Therma-Tru doors may be priced slightly higher due to their extensive design options and advanced features. Codel doors, while potentially more affordable, still offer high-quality performance and durability.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Installation considerations should also be taken into account, as both brands may require professional installation to ensure optimal performance and warranty coverage. Homeowners should consult with local contractors to understand the installation process and associated costs.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="How Do Costs Compare Between These Fiberglass Entry Doors?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">When comparing costs, it’s essential to consider both the initial investment and long-term value. Therma-Tru doors typically range from $1,000 to $2,500, depending on the model and features. Codel doors may be priced between $800 and $1,800, offering a more budget-friendly option without compromising quality.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Ultimately, the choice between Therma-Tru and Codel doors will depend on individual preferences, budget, and specific needs.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="What Are the Installation and Maintenance Requirements?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Both Therma-Tru and Codel doors require minimal maintenance, making them convenient options for busy homeowners. Regular cleaning and occasional inspections are recommended to ensure longevity.</p>[/et_pb_text][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Installation should be performed by professionals familiar with the specific requirements of each brand to guarantee proper fit and function. Homeowners should follow the manufacturer's guidelines for maintenance to keep their doors looking and performing their best.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Frequently Asked Questions" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h2" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading] [et_pb_heading title="What is the main difference between Therma-Tru and Codel doors?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Therma-Tru is a premium national brand known for extensive style options, industry certifications, and a long track record in fiberglass entry doors. Codel is a value-oriented manufacturer offering solid fiberglass construction at a lower price point, making it a popular choice for budget-conscious homeowners and builders.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Are Therma-Tru doors worth the higher price compared to Codel?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Therma-Tru doors are generally worth the premium for homeowners prioritizing design variety, energy efficiency certifications (ENERGY STAR), and long-term durability. Codel doors offer excellent value for standard installations where budget is the primary concern.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Which fiberglass entry door brand offers better energy efficiency - Therma-Tru or Codel?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Therma-Tru doors typically carry ENERGY STAR certification and publish detailed U-factor and Solar Heat Gain Coefficient (SHGC) ratings. Codel doors also provide good insulation for the price, but Therma-Tru generally leads in published energy performance data and third-party certifications.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Do Therma-Tru and Codel doors come with warranties?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Yes. Therma-Tru offers a limited lifetime warranty on the door slab, covering defects in materials and workmanship. Codel also provides warranty coverage on their fiberglass doors, though terms may vary by product line. Always verify current warranty details with the manufacturer or retailer before purchasing.</p>[/et_pb_text] [et_pb_heading title="Can I install a Therma-Tru or Codel door myself, or do I need a professional?" _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" title_level="h3" hover_enabled="0" sticky_enabled="0"][/et_pb_heading][et_pb_text _builder_version="4.27.6" _module_preset="default" global_colors_info="{}"]<p class="metasyncPara">Both Therma-Tru and Codel doors can be installed by experienced DIYers, but professional installation is recommended to ensure proper sealing, weatherproofing, and warranty compliance. Improper installation can void warranties and reduce energy efficiency performance.</p>[/et_pb_text][/et_pb_column][/et_pb_row][/et_pb_section]

